-- title:
--   Toric points lie in the finite part
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0$ nonzero and $p$ a nonzero prime, together with a hypothesis $hpN_0$ that $p \nmid N_0$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `A.nonunits`. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData N₀ p A`, that is: a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over `base p` carrying a relative group law, and bijections identifying $J_0(N_0)$-points, respectively $J_0(N_0)$-points over the residue field of $A$, with sections of $X$ over the generic and the residual point. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`: a smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact, surjective group scheme $g \colon G \to$ `base p` with connected fibres, a commutative relative group law, a Galois- and Hecke-equivariant additive identification of $J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}) =$ `JZero (N₀ * p)` with sections over the generic point, flatness and surjectivity of all positive multiplication-by-$n$ maps, properness of the generic fibre, a toric rank and the remaining data of that structure. Then for every natural number $m$ one has $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m \le O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ as subgroups of `JZero (N₀ * p)`: the subgroup generated by the range of the toric points $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$ (and the trivial subgroup when $m = 0$) is contained in the subgroup generated by those $x$ which lie in `jZeroTorsion (N₀ * p) m` and for which the section $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ satisfies `ExtendsToPlace A Λ.σA`.
--
--   This is the inclusion of the toric part of the $m$-torsion into the part that extends over the valuation subring $A$, i.e. the statement that toric torsion points of $J_0(N_0p)$ at $p$ belong to the finite part; in the classical treatment it is part of the analysis of the torus of the reduction of $J_0(N_0p)$ at $p$ used in level lowering. It supplies the corresponding field of the Néron-data structure and is used in the study of the monodromy span inside the Tate module of `JZero`, and in the construction of the Néron data for the relevant newforms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_toricPts_le_finPts.lean

